Subject: [PATCH 1/1] kconfig: restore the upstream %_defconfig rule

ASUS replaced the upstream %_defconfig rule with one that concatenates the
defconfig with a per-project file:

    vendor/asus/bsp/${TARGET_PROJECT}/${TARGET_PROJECT}_diffconfig

That file is not part of the published source drop, and neither is anything
else under vendor/asus/bsp.  The rule also needs ANDROID_BUILD_TOP and OUT,
which only exist inside an Android build.  The net effect is that no
"make <something>_defconfig" works in a plain checkout -- it dies with

    /bin/sh: 1: cannot create /merge_config.tmp: Permission denied

and arch/arm64/configs holds no defconfig for this SoC family anyway, so
there is nothing to merge the missing diffconfig into.

We do not need it.  asus_P00I_defconfig is a complete configuration,
recovered from the running kernel's own /proc/config.gz (the kernel is built
with CONFIG_IKCONFIG=y) and reduced with savedefconfig.  It round-trips back
to that configuration exactly, so the diffconfig has nothing left to add.

Restoring the upstream rule is therefore the whole fix.
---
 scripts/kconfig/Makefile | 5 +----
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git scripts/kconfig/Makefile scripts/kconfig/Makefile
index cb1b37ad..844bc9da 100644
--- scripts/kconfig/Makefile
+++ scripts/kconfig/Makefile
@@ -102,10 +102,7 @@ else
 endif
 
 %_defconfig: $(obj)/conf
-	@echo " Make kernel configs with diffconfig ++"
-	cat $(ANDROID_BUILD_TOP)/kernel/arch/$(SRCARCH)/configs/$@ $(ANDROID_BUILD_TOP)/vendor/asus/bsp/${TARGET_PROJECT}/${TARGET_PROJECT}_diffconfig > $(OUT)/merge_config.tmp
-	$(Q)$< --defconfig=$(OUT)/merge_config.tmp $(Kconfig)
-	@echo " Make kernel configs with diffconfig --"
+	$(Q)$< --defconfig=arch/$(SRCARCH)/configs/$@ $(Kconfig)
 
 # Help text used by make help
 help:
